{"team":"WAS","col":"#F2C15A","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":61.8,"adot":7.9,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Ground-First Machine</h2><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 62% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (91% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p><strong>Jayden Daniels</strong> is a scramble threat \u2014 he takes off on <strong>6.7%</strong> of dropbacks (nearly double the 3.3% norm), rushing production that both lifts his own yardage and siphons a few carries from the backfield.</p><p><strong>Chig Okonkwo</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>18%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 47% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>run-first</strong> (42% pass), funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Jacory Croskey-Merritt</strong>. And with the TE commanding 18% of targets, <strong>Chig Okonkwo</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 68 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>143 rushing</strong> and <strong>233 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.81/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.51/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.35/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 46% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>Jacory Croskey-Merritt</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts; <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line; <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jayden Daniels","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":24,"props":{"Comp":17.88,"Att":26.94,"Pass Yds":192.27,"Pass TD":1.34,"INT":0.41,"Rush Yds":41.48},"d":{"completions":17.88,"attempts":26.94,"pass_yards":192.27,"pass_td":1.34,"interceptions":0.41,"rush_att":7.67,"rush_yards":41.48}}],"RB":[{"name":"Jacory Croskey-Merritt","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":35,"props":{"Rush Att":15.9,"Rush Yds":70.22,"Tgt":2.08,"Rec":1.57,"Rec Yds":11.38},"d":{"rush_att":15.9,"rush_yards":70.22,"targets":2.08,"receptions":1.57,"rec_yards":11.38,"rec_td":0.03}},{"name":"Rachaad White","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":21,"props":{"Rush Att":4.64,"Rush Yds":17.73,"Tgt":3.74,"Rec":2.78,"Rec Yds":19.38},"d":{"rush_att":4.64,"rush_yards":17.73,"targets":3.74,"receptions":2.78,"rec_yards":19.38,"rec_td":0.13}},{"name":"Kaytron Allen","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":13,"props":{"Rush Att":3.76,"Rush Yds":16.06,"Tgt":1.1,"Rec":0.73,"Rec Yds":5.28},"d":{"rush_att":3.76,"rush_yards":16.06,"targets":1.1,"receptions":0.73,"rec_yards":5.28,"rec_td":0.02}}],"WR":[{"name":"Terry McLaurin","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":26,"props":{"Tgt":8.16,"Rec":5.17,"Rec Yds":70.9,"Rec TD":0.29},"d":{"targets":8.16,"receptions":5.17,"rec_yards":70.9,"rec_td":0.29}},{"name":"Stefon Diggs","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":19,"props":{"Tgt":6.5,"Rec":4.56,"Rec Yds":53.42,"Rec TD":0.21},"d":{"targets":6.5,"receptions":4.56,"rec_yards":53.